<title>MALAYSIA: Seal asks for stock suspension.</title>
<headline>Seal asks for stock suspension.</headline>
<dateline>KUALA LUMPUR 1997-06-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Malaysian timber products firm Seal Inc Bhd on Thursday requested the Kuala Lumpur Stock Exchange to suspend its stock pending a news announcement.</p>
<p>The company did not give other details in its one-paragraph statement to the stock exchange.</p>
<p>The stock ended trading on Thursday at 4.88 ringgit, up 10 cents on volume of 1.74 million shares traded.</p>
<p>-- Kuala Lumpur newsroom (603-201 4813)</p>
